summary:
  Any failed load on a Cast receiver makes the widget say the device
  refused the station's address and that another station may work.

history:
  "… cannot play this station. The device refused this station's address.
  Another station may work." has to be true of every device that is told
  so. For a renderer's UPnP 716 it was measured: the same Ruark played
  another address minutes later (2026-11-12). What a television means by
  the codes of a failed load has not been seen on a device: one that is
  busy with another programme may answer the same way, and no other
  station would work on it either. Until that is measured the widget
  keeps "Could not cast to …" for it.

target:
  package/contents/ui/CastLogic.js

find:
      if (_REFUSALS[f.upnp] === true && (f.action === "SetAVTransportURI" || f.action === "Play"))

replace:
      if (f.load !== "" || _REFUSALS[f.upnp] === true && (f.action === "SetAVTransportURI" || f.action === "Play"))

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_castlogic.qml::test_what_an_answer_says.
